      "summaries": {
        "en": "Blender-MCP is an open-source tool that bridges Blender's 3D modeling capabilities with AI agents through the Model Context Protocol, enabling automated 3D scene manipulation. Its technical innovation lies in exposing Blender's Python API as structured endpoints that AI systems can reliably call, treating 3D operations as programmable functions. Developers can integrate it into AI workflows to generate scenes, modify objects, or create animations programmatically, making 3D content creation accessible to automated systems.",
        "zh": "Blender-MCP是一个开源工具，通过模型上下文协议将Blender的3D建模功能与AI智能体连接起来，实现自动化3D场景操作。其技术核心是将Blender的Python API封装为结构化端点，使AI系统能够可靠调用各种3D操作，将复杂的建模任务转化为可编程函数。开发者可将其集成到AI工作流中，用于程序化生成场景、修改物体或创建动画，为自动化内容创作提供了新的可能性。该项目展示了如何通过标准化接口让传统专业软件与新兴AI系统协同工作。",
        "es": "Blender-MCP is an open-source tool that bridges Blender's 3D modeling capabilities with AI agents through the Model Context Protocol, enabling automated 3D scene manipulation. Its technical innovation lies in exposing Blender's Python API as structured endpoints that AI systems can reliably call, treating 3D operations as programmable functions. Developers can integrate it into AI workflows to generate scenes, modify objects, or create animations programmatically, making 3D content creation accessible to automated systems.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "blender-mcp gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "Blender-MCP is an open-source tool that bridges Blender's 3D modeling capabilities with AI agents through the Model Context Protocol, enabling automated 3D scene manipulation. Its technical innovation lies in exposing Blender's Python API as structured endpoints that AI systems can reliably call, treating 3D operations as programmable functions. Developers can integrate it into AI workflows to generate scenes, modify objects, or create animations programmatically, making 3D content creation accessible to automated systems.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/ahujasid/blender-mcp for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
